# STM32F4 boot/connect smoke test. Brings up the Renode stm32f4
# backend end-to-end: the local stm32f4.repl (upstream stm32f4.repl +
# ADC1/2/3) plus upstream Miscellaneous.STM32F4_RCC is the F4-specific
# path - distinct from the F1 path (stm32f103_smoke, local rcc_stub)
# and the G0/H7 paths. printers.test reaches F4 chips via SKR-Pro /
# Octopus-class boards at config-parse depth; this is the firmware-boot
# regression target. Uses the stm32f446 build (F401/F405/F407/F446 all
# share stm32f4.repl; F446 is the most common 3D-printer-board variant).
DICTIONARY stm32f446.dict
CONFIG stm32f4_smoke.cfg
EMULATOR stm32f4_smoke.fixture.json

# A few harmless gcode lines so klippy gets past klippy:ready.
M114
M105
M105
M105

# klippy connected and stayed connected long enough to do the
# clocksync handshake against the TIM2-driven firmware clock.
EXPECT_LOG_CONTAINS "Loaded MCU 'mcu'"
EXPECT_LOG_NOT_CONTAINS "Internal error"
EXPECT_LOG_NOT_CONTAINS "Klippy is shutdown"
